digraph ReasoningTree {
  rankdir="TB";
  "N104" [label="(4,0,0) Currently insect-borne rice viruses can cause sporadic devastating epidemics whose origins are often unclear."];
  "N107" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Given rice is globally important and suffers large, hard-to-prevent insect-borne viral epidemics with unclear origins, therefore rice systems require improved, systematic virus discovery/surveillance."];
  "N205" [label="(0,0,0) If epidemics have unclear origins and there is evidence of spillover/reservoirs and novel virus-like signals in the host, then a likely explanation is that additional, previously uncharacterized viruses (including asymptomatic or reservoir-derived) exist and contribute to emergence risk."];
  "N301" [label="(11,0,0) Currently viral metagenomics can uncover hidden viruses without prior knowledge and can reconstruct (near-)complete genomes to characterize viral diversity."];
  "N308" [label="(0,0,0) If (i) large public RNA-seq resources likely contain viral reads and (ii) metagenomics plus RdRP-based and homology-independent methods can detect both known and divergent RNA viruses, then systematically mining public RNA-seq with both method classes is a feasible strategy for comprehensive RNA virus discovery."];
  "N401" [label="(18,0,0) Currently rice metagenomic virus studies have been limited by small sample sizes, restricting virus identification scope."];
  "N407" [label="(0,0,0) If a domain has abundant public RNA-seq data that has not been systematically mined and prior studies were underpowered, then a large-scale systematic analysis (potentially using Serratus to pre-screen) is justified to fill the discovery gap."];
  "N501" [label="(25,0,0) Currently rice is threatened by fungi and insect pests; and identifying viruses associated with these organisms could inform innovative prevention strategies."];
  "N502" [label="(0,0,0) If virus discovery in the rice agroecosystem includes viruses linked to pests/fungi, then the resulting virome knowledge can potentially support broader plant protection strategy development (beyond direct rice viruses)."];
  "N503" [label="(0,0,0) abduction-reasoning: Given rice faces fungi and insect pests and virus discovery could include viruses associated with them, therefore the virome study scope should include viruses potentially associated with rice, insects, and fungi in the rice ecosystem."];
  "N801" [label="(0,0,0) If (a) rice needs improved virus discovery/surveillance, (b) hidden/unknown rice-associated viruses likely exist, (c) systematic public-RNA-seq mining with complementary methods is feasible, and (d) a major rice-specific data gap exists, then the best research plan is a large-scale systematic mining of public rice RNA-seq across Oryza using homology-based + homology-independent detection and Serratus-guided screening, followed by assembly/annotation/classification and association screening."];
  "N839" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Given the proposal statement is established and should be represented as the root node, therefore the root node is that proposal statement."];
  "N841" [label="(0,0,0) If the root node is that proposal statement, then the single root node content should be the final research proposal."];
  "N843" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Given the root node is that proposal statement, therefore the root node content is the final research proposal."];
  "N845" [label="(0,0,0) If the final mapped root content is the research proposal statement, then the final conclusion node should be that proposal statement."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This paper proposes to develop and evaluate a large-scale rice virome-mining framework that analyzes publicly available Oryza RNA-seq libraries with homology-based, RdRP/Serratus-guided, and homology-independent methods to assemble, annotate, classify, quantify, and prioritize RNA viruses relevant to rice ecosystem surveillance.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When disease burden, hidden-virus signals, feasible public-data mining methods, an underused RNA-seq resource, ecosystem relevance, and an explicit operational workflow converge, they jointly motivate a cautious paper-level proposal to systematically mine rice RNA-seq for RNA-virus discovery and surveillance."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Because the established root content is the research proposal, the final conclusion should restate that established proposal rather than add a new evidentiary claim."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) Unclear rice-virus epidemic origins, wild-plant reservoir/spillover evidence, novel rice-associated viruses, and calls to reassess virus breadth indicate hidden components of rice ecosystem viromes."];
  "R15" [label="(0,0,0) These hidden-virome and cross-compartment signals make additional uncharacterized rice-associated viruses a plausible explanation and discovery target."];
  "R16" [label="(0,0,0) Public sequencing resources and viral discovery toolchains provide complementary routes for detecting RNA viruses, including known, RdRP-detectable, and highly divergent candidates."];
  "R17" [label="(0,0,0) Systematic mining of public rice RNA-seq with metagenomic, RdRP-based, and homology-independent approaches is feasible for broad RNA-virus detection."];
  "R18" [label="(0,0,0) Rice virome discovery has a resource-and-method gap: many public rice RNA-seq libraries remain systematically unmined, prior studies were small, and Serratus RdRP signals require deeper assembly and annotation."];
  "R19" [label="(0,0,0) The rice RNA-seq resource-and-method gap justifies a large-scale systematic virome analysis using Serratus-guided screening followed by deeper assembly and annotation."];
  "R22" [label="(0,0,0) The converging premises for the study are surveillance need, likely hidden rice-associated viruses, feasible public-RNA-seq virus mining, an underused rice RNA-seq resource, broader rice-ecosystem relevance, and alignment with the concrete study plan."];
  "R23" [label="(0,0,0) Given those converging premises, a comprehensive large-scale, multi-method mining of public rice RNA-seq is warranted and actionable."];
  "R30" [label="(0,0,0) The root node should contain the established final research proposal rather than a separate formal aggregation statement."];
  "N501" -> "N503" [label="abduction-phenomenon"];
